1
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:11,090
I love traveling abroad. I love Japan's cherry blossoms and shrines.

2
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:13,972
I prefer online games and figurines.

3
00:00:14,010 --> 00:00:16,707
I also play games at home

4
00:00:16,890 --> 00:00:19,049
And collect some figurines.

5
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:21,050
Don't you find it interesting?

6
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:25,640
Wow, I'm hopeless at games.

7
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:26,640
I don't know how to play at all.

8
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,630
I can teach you how to play games

9
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:30,918
My Switch is still collecting dust.

10
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:34,582
Really?

11
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,500
I want to play

12
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:37,510
I'll bring it next time.

13
00:00:37,510 --> 00:00:38,510
We could get Pokémon.

14
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:40,978
Wow

15
00:00:40,990 --> 00:00:43,219
But I really like

16
00:00:43,230 --> 00:00:45,230
collecting those perfumes and shoes

17
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:47,220
Because I think they're unique

18
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:49,220
I don't really get that

19
00:00:49,230 --> 00:00:50,230
But I like listening to pop music

20
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:52,220
I think pop music is unique too

21
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:54,956
Hmm, that's true

22
00:00:54,970 --> 00:00:56,970
But I prefer classical music

23
00:00:56,970 --> 00:00:58,960
What's so good about classical music?

24
00:00:58,970 --> 00:01:00,200
You like to eat...

25
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:01,240
I'm a bank manager

26
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:03,150
Now we're suddenly talking about jobs.

27
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:04,150
I'm a security guard

28
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:07,200
Brecht?

29
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:15,550
No more Brecht.

30
00:01:15,550 --> 00:01:16,640
These...

31
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:18,640
Is it possible to combine these two?

32
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:20,810
Just say it straight to her.

33
00:01:20,810 --> 00:01:26,680
How am I supposed to make myself clear to you?

34
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:27,870
Right?

35
00:01:27,870 --> 00:01:28,910
How does that feel to you?

36
00:01:28,910 --> 00:01:31,910
Hmm

37
00:01:33,313 --> 00:01:37,823
Think it over.

38
00:01:37,823 --> 00:01:41,331
I can secretly watch the monitors

39
00:01:41,343 --> 00:01:43,473
I can see you anytime

40
00:01:43,473 --> 00:01:45,489
Don't you feel safe?

41
00:01:45,513 --> 00:01:46,853
It gives me a sense of security.

42
00:01:46,853 --> 00:01:48,273
Then can I install one

43
00:01:48,273 --> 00:01:49,413
in your security booth too?

44
00:01:49,413 --> 00:01:50,533
I'll watch you anytime too

45
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:53,543
But if, in that security booth,

46
00:01:53,543 --> 00:01:57,243
you put on a show every day—

47
00:01:57,243 --> 00:01:58,203
if you performed—

48
00:01:58,203 --> 00:01:59,503
that might be interesting.

49
00:01:59,503 --> 00:02:00,923
If you're just sitting there

50
00:02:00,923 --> 00:02:02,063
I can perform for you

51
00:02:02,063 --> 00:02:03,703
We can video call all day

52
00:02:03,703 --> 00:02:04,863
I have plenty of time

53
00:02:04,863 --> 00:02:05,683
But I still have to work

54
00:02:05,683 --> 00:02:08,003
You can watch whenever you want

55
00:02:08,003 --> 00:02:09,443
Call me and I'll be there

56
00:02:09,443 --> 00:02:10,963
I have my own security booth

57
00:02:10,963 --> 00:02:12,813
Let's drop that.

58
00:02:12,813 --> 00:02:13,613
Do you own a place?

59
00:02:13,613 --> 00:02:18,613
I rent a 20-square-meter apartment

60
00:02:18,613 --> 00:02:22,913
I agree, I agree.

61
00:02:22,913 --> 00:02:25,043
I totally agree.

62
00:02:25,073 --> 00:02:26,153
Oh, exactly!

63
00:02:26,153 --> 00:02:27,183
Oh!

64
00:02:27,193 --> 00:02:28,453
No—

65
00:02:28,453 --> 00:02:29,793
Be a bit sarcastic

66
00:02:29,793 --> 00:02:31,033
What are you doing?

67
00:02:31,033 --> 00:02:32,673
You still don't believe it.

68
00:02:32,673 --> 00:02:34,323
That's exactly right.

69
00:02:34,323 --> 00:02:34,883
Perfect.

70
00:02:34,883 --> 00:02:35,463
What do you want now?

71
00:02:35,463 --> 00:02:37,363
Wow, a whole twenty square metres!

72
00:02:37,363 --> 00:02:38,163
Right, right.

73
00:02:38,163 --> 00:02:38,663
Exactly.

74
00:02:38,663 --> 00:02:40,263
Twenty square metres!

75
00:02:40,263 --> 00:02:41,703
Exactly.

76
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:43,583
Wow, so huge!

77
00:02:43,583 --> 00:02:45,203
Right—keep going.

78
00:02:45,203 --> 00:02:47,083
Just enough for me.

79
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:48,523
Enough for both of us?

80
00:02:48,523 --> 00:02:50,233
Sure—one bedroom, one living room, one bathroom.

81
00:02:50,243 --> 00:02:52,523
I also have a soft double bed

82
00:02:52,523 --> 00:02:55,523
Yeah. Enough room for two pairs of slippers?

83
00:02:55,523 --> 00:02:56,403
Is there?

84
00:02:56,403 --> 00:02:57,563
Two pairs of slippers

85
00:02:57,563 --> 00:02:58,723
Ask it deadpan.

86
00:02:58,723 --> 00:02:59,403
There is.

87
00:02:59,403 --> 00:03:02,293
Haha

88
00:03:02,303 --> 00:03:04,183
[unclear]—how did that come through?

89
00:03:04,203 --> 00:03:05,043
Do you have a car?

90
00:03:05,043 --> 00:03:06,323
Yes

91
00:03:06,323 --> 00:03:09,323
I have an old-fashioned bicycle

92
00:03:09,323 --> 00:03:10,683
The kind with a crossbar

93
00:03:10,683 --> 00:03:11,523
Now I agree even more.

94
00:03:11,523 --> 00:03:14,003
I can take you to and from work.

95
00:03:14,003 --> 00:03:15,693
I love bicycles.

96
00:03:15,703 --> 00:03:16,523
Exactly.

97
00:03:16,523 --> 00:03:18,523
When I was little, my grandpa carried me

98
00:03:18,523 --> 00:03:21,043
on his bike to kindergarten.

99
00:03:21,043 --> 00:03:22,283
Ha

100
00:03:22,283 --> 00:03:25,769
Maybe you can take me back to childhood

101
00:03:25,843 --> 00:03:26,873
Your bike has a back seat, right?

102
00:03:26,883 --> 00:03:27,243
Right?

103
00:03:27,243 --> 00:03:28,083
Of course

104
00:03:28,083 --> 00:03:29,043
If you don't want the seat,

105
00:03:29,043 --> 00:03:30,243
You can sit on my lap

106
00:03:30,243 --> 00:03:31,483
You can sit on that crossbar too

107
00:03:31,483 --> 00:03:32,163
Now I really agree.

108
00:03:32,163 --> 00:03:33,083
Oh!

109
00:03:33,083 --> 00:03:33,843
Amazing!

110
00:03:33,843 --> 00:03:34,873
Lucky me!

111
00:03:35,043 --> 00:03:37,363
Is that some special trick of yours?

112
00:03:37,363 --> 00:03:38,363
Exactly.

113
00:03:38,363 --> 00:03:40,233
Wow, a man of hidden talents.

114
00:03:40,243 --> 00:03:43,323
You can hold me and still ride?

115
00:03:43,323 --> 00:03:44,813
You'd be riding...

116
00:03:44,813 --> 00:03:47,153
How does that work?

117
00:03:47,153 --> 00:03:48,593
After our date,

118
00:03:48,593 --> 00:03:50,304
I'll take you for a ride.

119
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:51,513
Oh, okay, okay.

120
00:03:51,513 --> 00:03:52,233
Oh, you...

121
00:03:53,713 --> 00:03:54,273
At her.

122
00:03:54,273 --> 00:03:55,863
You're going to insult her, right?

123
00:03:55,863 --> 00:03:57,033
Anything goes. Insult her—go.

124
00:03:57,043 --> 00:04:01,693
Aren't you good at that?

125
00:04:01,693 --> 00:04:03,233
How come you've got nothing to say now?

126
00:04:03,233 --> 00:04:04,873
What's going on?

127
00:04:04,873 --> 00:04:05,863
Why?

128
00:04:05,863 --> 00:04:07,423
Do you really think

129
00:04:07,423 --> 00:04:09,613
I'd believe that?

130
00:04:09,613 --> 00:04:11,153
Not enough. Not enough. Not enough.

131
00:04:11,153 --> 00:04:13,283
Do you honestly think I

132
00:04:13,373 --> 00:04:16,383
really agree with you that much?

133
00:04:16,473 --> 00:04:18,513
You don't?

134
00:04:18,513 --> 00:04:19,573
You're only saying that because...

135
00:04:19,573 --> 00:04:21,673
Don't you think she's wonderful?

136
00:04:21,673 --> 00:04:23,413
For you.

137
00:04:23,413 --> 00:04:27,493
I don't want to sit on a bicycle

138
00:04:27,493 --> 00:04:28,813
with you holding me.

139
00:04:28,813 --> 00:04:30,933
I'm worried I'll fall off.

140
00:04:30,933 --> 00:04:32,543
I don't want to squeeze in with you

141
00:04:32,543 --> 00:04:34,183
in a twenty-square-metre apartment

142
00:04:34,183 --> 00:04:36,223
with room for only two pairs of slippers.

143
00:04:36,223 --> 00:04:38,303
You could fit your sneakers too.

144
00:04:38,303 --> 00:04:39,763
I have a shoe rack.

145
00:04:39,803 --> 00:04:41,343
I want a yard,

146
00:04:41,343 --> 00:04:43,043
where I can keep a dog and a cat,

147
00:04:43,043 --> 00:04:44,213
Can you do that?

148
00:04:44,243 --> 00:04:49,423
But weren't you

149
00:04:49,423 --> 00:04:51,383
just talking to me so nicely?

150
00:04:51,383 --> 00:04:53,733
How else

151
00:04:53,733 --> 00:04:55,273
would you have believed me?

152
00:04:55,273 --> 00:04:57,413
You're so naive.

153
00:04:57,503 --> 00:05:00,063
But you only have eight hours,

154
00:05:00,063 --> 00:05:01,363
I'm trying to save you,

155
00:05:01,363 --> 00:05:03,503
You're about to be restarted.

156
00:05:03,643 --> 00:05:08,203
I think...

157
00:05:08,203 --> 00:05:10,740
Even if I get restarted,

158
00:05:10,823 --> 00:05:12,643
I still wouldn't be with you.

159
00:05:12,933 --> 00:05:13,893
A loser.

160
00:05:13,893 --> 00:05:16,653
Why does "loser" sound so mild?

161
00:05:16,653 --> 00:05:17,853
Yeah, it isn't harsh enough.

162
00:05:17,853 --> 00:05:18,693
Really?

163
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:22,303
[unclear]—you're just...

164
00:05:22,303 --> 00:05:24,043
You're a fucking idiot.

165
00:05:24,043 --> 00:05:27,433
You're a loser.

166
00:05:27,433 --> 00:05:29,783
"Fucking idiot" sounds mild too.

167
00:05:29,783 --> 00:05:31,723
You're a hick.

168
00:05:31,723 --> 00:05:35,835
"Hick" doesn't sound mild.

169
00:05:35,853 --> 00:05:38,200
"Hick" doesn't sound mild.

170
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:40,120
I'm doing just fine, aren't I?

171
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:42,160
Waiter, get me a steak.

172
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:44,090
The waiter comes over all smarmy:

173
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:44,740
What did he say?

174
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:46,700
Sorry, sir, this is a couples' restaurant,

175
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:47,540
we don't sell half portions.

176
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:52,071
Then you lose it and start swearing.

177
00:05:52,130 --> 00:05:53,880
"Bullshit! Fuck your mom!"

178
00:05:53,890 --> 00:05:57,050
What? I'm on a date, aren't I?

179
00:05:57,050 --> 00:05:58,570
Then who the fuck is that in front of me?

180
00:05:58,570 --> 00:06:01,160
The waiter says, "Sir, wake up—

181
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,120
that's you."

182
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:05,390
So you can use that mirror.

183
00:06:05,390 --> 00:06:06,420
Those mirrors can...

184
00:06:08,953 --> 00:06:11,313
These questions have never crossed my mind.

185
00:06:11,313 --> 00:06:12,703
I don't know how to respond.

186
00:06:12,713 --> 00:06:14,953
Honestly, I don't understand him at all.

187
00:06:14,953 --> 00:06:18,073
After he asked those questions,

188
00:06:18,073 --> 00:06:24,233
he felt like a stranger to me.

189
00:06:24,233 --> 00:06:27,223
Like a poor little animal, soaked by the roadside.

190
00:06:27,233 --> 00:06:30,233
Leave me there and your conscience will condemn you.

191
00:06:30,233 --> 00:06:32,223
Yeah, yeah, I think that's it.

192
00:06:32,233 --> 00:06:34,233
Maybe my perspective leans more toward...

193
00:06:34,243 --> 00:06:35,243
seeing her as a little animal.

194
00:06:35,243 --> 00:06:38,243
Because we're discussing the female viewer's perspective, right?

195
00:06:38,243 --> 00:06:40,300
But I think my perspective leans more toward...

196
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:42,780
He's very innocent—not as mature as you all.

197
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:44,780
It's different from women's and men's perspectives.

198
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:47,170
I feel like this guy

199
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:49,680
came into this conversation thinking,

200
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,670
"This relationship feels unequal to me."

201
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:54,480
It's not about imbalance. His love is pure.

202
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:57,480
It is unequal. It definitely is.

203
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,480
It's just that I love you, but you don't love me as much.

204
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:01,480
You don't love me the way I love you.

205
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:02,480
To me, that's an imbalance.

206
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:04,867
That's his way of seeking love.

207
00:07:06,837 --> 00:07:07,987
Never validates me.

208
00:07:07,987 --> 00:07:15,037
Always acts so superior.

209
00:07:15,037 --> 00:07:15,467
Sometimes—

210
00:07:15,467 --> 00:07:18,267
Because of pressure, insecurity, things like that...

211
00:07:18,267 --> 00:07:21,877
Yeah, your family is so well-off—you're a rich kid.

212
00:07:21,877 --> 00:07:23,397
Why would you want me?

213
00:07:23,397 --> 00:07:25,597
There are so many great girls out there.

214
00:07:25,597 --> 00:07:30,507
Once I choose to be with you,

215
00:07:30,507 --> 00:07:33,677
I feel a sense of responsibility.

216
00:07:33,677 --> 00:07:35,877
No matter what happens,

217
00:07:35,877 --> 00:07:38,697
unless I turn out to be a scumbag

218
00:07:38,697 --> 00:07:41,557
and run off with somebody else.

219
00:07:41,557 --> 00:07:45,197
I'm not really that rich.

220
00:07:45,197 --> 00:07:48,739
What I can do for you right now

221
00:07:49,017 --> 00:07:49,977
is honestly

222
00:07:49,977 --> 00:07:52,534
the most

223
00:07:52,547 --> 00:07:53,637
I can give.

224
00:07:53,637 --> 00:07:56,267
I've never asked you for anything.

225
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:58,327
I've never once said,

226
00:07:58,327 --> 00:08:00,807
"You're my girlfriend.
You should give me gifts."

227
00:08:00,807 --> 00:08:03,267
We just started dating.
